course: dictionary
lesson: 10394
title: Shapes in words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. Triangular describes a shape with three sides and three corners, but in maths it can also describe a number pattern. «A triangular flag flapped on the mast.» The clue is flag: you can picture the shape straight away.
explain: «Triangular numbers are 1, 3, 6, 10 and 15.» The numbers tell you this is the maths meaning: a number of dots that can be arranged in a triangle. Always ask: what do the words around this one show me?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. Swap in "shaped like a triangle" and check that it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Triangular means shaped like a triangle, with three sides and three corners.
fact: A triangular number is a number of dots that can make a triangle: 1, 3, 6, 10, 15 and so on.
fact: «In the UK and much of Europe, triangular signs warn» drivers of danger ahead.
fact: Context clues can show you which meaning of a word is needed.
fact: The Portuguese and Spanish used caravels with «triangular lateen sails» that could sail closer to the wind.
exercise: «A triangular flag flapped on the mast.» What is triangular describing? | The mast | *The shape of the flag, which has three sides | A flag | The wind
exercise: «Triangular numbers are 1, 3, 6, 10 and 15.» What kind of meaning is triangular here? | A kind of sandwich | *A number of dots that can make a triangle | A loud noise | A shape with four sides
exercise: Dad says his sandwiches are cut into «triangular» pieces. What do the pieces look like? | *Three sides and three corners | A circle | A square | A long straight line
test: «The shoulder blade is a flat triangular bone.» What does flat triangular mean? | Soft and squashy | Very hot | *Flat and shaped like a triangle, with three sides and three corners | Round and thick
test: Which of these is a triangular number? | *6 | 8 | 4 | 9
exam: Which number is NOT a triangular number? | *7 | 1 | 3 | 6
